{"The enableSqlExpressions function always returns false regardless of the feature flag state - both the if enabled branch and the fall-through return false, making the feature flag check dead code. The inverted logic (!IsEnabledGlobally) combined with the misleading variable name 'enabled' creates a trap where a future developer 'fixing' this could accidentally re-enable the RCE vulnerability": 0.9067138433456421, "The new in-memory SQL DB stub returns generic 'not implemented' errors, which upstream code treats/logs as 'invalid sql query'; when legacy parsing paths are used, users can get misleading validation errors even though the feature is intentionally disabled": 0.7149750590324402}